given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanety</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Bashan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prolonged oxidative stress impairs insulin-induced GLUT4 translocation in 3T3-L1 adipocytes</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><year>1998</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>1562</fpage><lpage>1569</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9753293</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diabetes.47.10.1562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hansen</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikeda</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsen</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Busch</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Mosthaf</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insulin signaling is inhibited by micromolar concentrations of H(2)O(2). Evidence for a role of H(2)O(2) in tumor necrosis factor alpha-mediated insulin resistance</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1999</year><volume>274</volume><fpage>25078</fpage><lpage>25084</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10455187</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.274.35.25078</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tirosh</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Potashnik</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bashan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudich</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxidative stress disrupts insulin-induced cellular redistribution of insulin receptor substrate-1 and phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase in 3T3-L1 adipocytes. A putative cellular mechanism for impaired protein kinase B activation and GLUT4 t